    {
      "server": "google_calendar",
      "tools": [
        {
          "tool_name": "google_calendar__search",
          "description": "Search for events in Google Calendar.\n\nUse time_min/time_max for time-based questions (\"what meetings do I have today\", \"schedule for next week\") — compute actual RFC3339 timestamps with the user's timezone offset from viewer context (e.g. 2026-05-20T00:00:00-07:00). Always include the offset.\n\nIMPORTANT — query is simple text matching, NOT a search engine:\n- Use a SINGLE keyword or short phrase (e.g. \"dentist\", \"team sync\"). Do NOT use OR, AND, NOT operators — they are matched literally and will return empty results.\n- Prefer time_min/time_max alone to list events in a range, then filter results yourself. Only add query when you need to narrow by a specific word in the event title/description.\n- If a search returns empty, retry with a broader time range or drop the query entirely.\n\nTo search another user's calendar, pass their email as calendar_id.\nEvents returned contain an event_id, which is required for other Google Calendar tools.",
          "score": 6.270590782165527,
          "input_schema": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "query": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Simple text match against event title, description, location, and attendees. Use a single keyword or short phrase (e.g. 'dentist', 'team sync'). Do NOT use OR/AND/NOT operators — they are matched literally. Omit to list all events in a time range."
              },
              "max_results": {
                "type": "integer",
                "description": "Maximum number of events to return (default 25, max 100)"
              },
              "time_min": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Start of time range (RFC3339 with timezone offset, e.g. 1970-01-31T12:00:00-08:00). Always include the user's timezone offset from viewer context."
              },
              "time_max": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "End of time range (RFC3339 with timezone offset, e.g. 1970-01-31T13:00:00-08:00). Always include the user's timezone offset from viewer context."
              },
              "calendar_id": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Calendar ID to search (e.g. email address from google_calendar_list_calendars). Defaults to the user's primary calendar."
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "server": "notion",
      "tools": [
        {
          "tool_name": "notion__notion-search",
          "description": "Search for pages, databases, and connected sources in the user's Notion workspace.\nPerforms semantic search over Notion content and connected sources (Slack, Google Drive, GitHub, Jira, Microsoft Teams, SharePoint, OneDrive, Linear). Connected source search requires a Notion AI plan; without it, search is limited to the Notion workspace only.\n\n## When to use this tool\n\n- ALWAYS call this BEFORE notion-fetch when the user references a Notion page by name, title, or topic. Do NOT guess or fabricate Notion page IDs.\n- ALWAYS call this when notion-fetch returns a validation_error -- the failed id was likely a page title or slug, not a valid UUID.\n- Use the `id` field from search results to call notion-fetch.\n- Use one search call per question for best results.\n\n## Parameters\n\n- `query` (required): Semantic search query -- must be at least 1 character. Use natural language describing what you are looking for. NEVER pass an empty string `\"\"`.\n- `filters` (required): Pass `{}` for no filters, or use:\n   - `created_date_range`: `{\"start_date\": \"2024-01-01\", \"end_date\": \"2025-01-01\"}`\n   - `created_by_user_ids`: `[\"user-uuid-1\", \"user-uuid-2\"]`\n- `page_size`: Max results (default 10, max 25). Do NOT exceed 25.\n- `max_highlight_length`: Max chars for result highlights (default 200, 0 to omit).\n- `page_url`: Restrict search to within a specific page and its sub-pages.\n- `teamspace_id`: Restrict search to a specific teamspace.\n- `data_source_url`: Search within a specific database data source (use `collection://...` URL from notion-fetch output, NOT the database URL).\n\n## Workflow: search then fetch\n\n1. Call notion-search with the user's query and `\"filters\": {}`.\n2. From the results, pick the matching page and take its `id` field.\n3. Call notion-fetch with that `id` -- it will be a valid UUID.\n\n<example description=\"Basic search\">{\"query\": \"weekly standup notes\", \"filters\": {}}</example>\n<example description=\"Date-filtered search\">{\"query\": \"quarterly revenue\", \"filters\": {\"created_date_range\": {\"start_date\":… [truncated]",
          "score": 3.879875421524048,
          "input_schema": {
            "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "query": {
                "type": "string",
                "minLength": 1,
                "description": "Semantic search query over your entire Notion workspace and connected sources (Slack, Google Drive, Github, Jira, Microsoft Teams, Sharepoint, OneDrive, or Linear). For best results, don't provide more than one question per tool call. Use a separate \"search\" tool call for each search you want to perform.\n\nAlternatively, the query can be a substring or keyword to find users by matching against their name or email address. For example: \"john\" or \"john@example.com\""
              },
              "query_type": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "internal",
                  "user"
                ]
              },
              "content_search_mode": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "workspace_search",
                  "ai_search"
                ]
              },
              "data_source_url": {
                "description": "Optionally, provide the URL of a Data source to search. This will perform a semantic search over the pages in the Data Source. Note: must be a Data Source, not a Database. <data-source> tags are part of the Notion flavored Markdown format returned by tools like fetch. The full spec is available in the create-pages tool description.",
                "type": "string"
              },
              "page_url": {
                "description": "Optionally, provide the URL or ID of a page to search within. This will perform a semantic search over the content within and under the specified page. Accepts either a full page URL (e.g. https://notion.so/workspace/Page-Title-1234567890) or just the page ID (UUIDv4) with or without dashes.",
                "type": "string"
              },
              "teamspace_id": {
                "description": "Optionally, provide the ID of a teamspace to restrict search results to. This will perform a search over content within the specified teamspace only. Accepts the teamspace ID (UUIDv4) with or without dashes.",
                "type": "string"
              },
              "filters": {
                "description": "Optionally provide filters to apply to the search results. Only valid when query_type is 'internal'.",
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "created_date_range": {
                    "description": "Optional filter to only produce search results created within the specified date range.",
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                      "start_date": {
                        "description": "The start date of the date range as an ISO 8601 date string, if any.",
                        "type": "string",
                        "format": "date",
                        "pattern": "^(?:(?:\\d\\d[2468][048]|\\d\\d[13579][26]|\\d\\d0[48]|[02468][048]00|[13579][26]00)-02-29|\\d{4}-(?:(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])|(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|30)|(?:02)-(?:0[1-9]|1\\d|2[0-8])))$"
                      },
                      "end_date": {
                        "description": "The end date of the date range as an ISO 8601 date string, if any.",
                        "type": "string",
                        "format": "date",
                        "pattern": "^(?:(?:\\d\\d[2468][048]|\\d\\d[13579][26]|\\d\\d0[48]|[02468][048]00|[13579][26]00)-02-29|\\d{4}-(?:(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])|(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|30)|(?:02)-(?:0[1-9]|1\\d|2[0-8])))$"
                      }
                    },
                    "additionalProperties": {}
                  },
                  "created_by_user_ids": {
                    "description": "Optional filter to only produce search results created by the Notion users that have the specified user IDs.",
                    "maxItems": 100,
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  }
                },
                "additionalProperties": {}
              },
              "page_size": {
                "description": "Maximum number of results to return (default 10). Lower values reduce response size.",
                "type": "integer",
                "minimum": 1,
                "maximum": 25
              },
              "max_highlight_length": {
                "description": "Maximum character length for result highlights (default 200). Set to 0 to omit highlights entirely.",
                "type": "integer",
                "minimum": 0,
                "maximum": 500
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "query"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": {}
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
